  "id": "f18ecbc1-8611-47e2-9b43-79077b3ff874",
  "title": "Visual Token Pruning in Vision-Language Models",
  "summary": "Visual Token Pruning Frameworks and Efficient Video Vision-Language Models aim to reduce inference costs while maintaining performance in multimodal and video-based tasks. These approaches include methods like SinkPruner, TReVS, MSDG-Prune, and V-CoLA, which focus on token selection and attention guidance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Visual Token Pruning Frameworks and Efficient Video Vision-Language Models aim to reduce inference costs while maintaining performance in multimodal and video-based tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SinkPruner and TReVS integrate text and visual features to prune visual tokens effectively.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SimpleComp provides a training-free baseline for video token compression with strong performance at most visual token retention ratios.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
